     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Abhishek Sharma Reportedly Seeking Exit From Sunrisers Hyderabad</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Sunrisers Hyderabad opener Abhishek Sharma is reportedly unhappy and seeking a departure from the franchise ahead of the IPL retention deadline. The player's dissatisfaction stems from Ishan Kishan being named captain last year, a role he is expected to retain for the 2027 season due to Pat Cummins reducing his franchise commitments.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/abhishek-sharma-reportedly-seeking-exit-from-sunrisers-hyder.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sharma is now linked to potential moves to the Mumbai Indians, Gujarat Titans, or Punjab Kings. Additionally, the Delhi Capitals have emerged as a possible destination for the star batter as he considers his future outside of Hyderabad.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the source's claims regarding the player's potential exit and the reasons behind it.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/cricket/ipl/top-stories/ipl-retentions-unhappy-abhishek-sharma-wants-to-leave-srh-but-where-will-he-go/articleshow/134638490.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/hyderabad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hyderabad</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
