       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by The Hindu, India Today">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Akash Anand Seeks Reinstatement to Bahujan Samaj Party</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>One month after his expulsion from the Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP), Akash Anand has publicly appealed to his aunt, party chief Mayawati, for a chance to serve the organization again. In a social media post, Anand described Mayawati as his political guru and inspiration while dismissing rumors that he would join other political parties.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/akash-anand-seeks-reinstatement-to-bahujan-samaj-party.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Anand, who was removed as national coordinator on September 10, 2026, apologized for past silence that led to misunderstandings. He emphasized that the BSP is his family and pledged to prove his commitment through hard work, despite offers from other parties like the Samajwadi Party and Nishad Party.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political appeal and the context of the expulsion while adhering to the word count constraints.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/uttar-pradesh/bsp-is-my-family-mayawatis-nephew-akash-anand-seeks-another-chance-after-expulsion/article71536904.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/akash-anand-bsp-national-convenor-mayawati-reappoints-nephew-after-ouster-3010269-2026-10-05?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
       
