       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Bandi Sanjay Criticizes Congress Over ECI Allegations</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister of State for Home Affairs Bandi Sanjay Kumar has accused the Congress party of tarnishing the Election Commission of India’s (ECI) reputation for political gain. Speaking in Karimnagar, Sanjay argued that attacking the constitutional body undermines democratic systems and misleads the public regarding the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/bandi-sanjay-criticizes-congress-over-eci-allegations.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sanjay challenged Congress to clarify its position on the removal of bogus, duplicate, and deceased entries from electoral rolls. He further alleged that the party is spreading false narratives and claimed that large numbers of illegal immigrants have been improperly enrolled as voters in regions such as the Maheshwaram Assembly constituency.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately summarizes the politician's statements and the specific regional allegations mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/bandi-sanjay-accuses-congress-of-mudslinging-against-eci/article71556918.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
