     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>CMC Vellore Hosts 11th International Cell and Gene Therapy Conference</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 11th International Cell and Gene Therapy Conference (CGTCON 2026) began October 8 at Christian Medical College in Vellore. Organized by the Centre for Stem Cell Research and inStem, the three-day event focuses on advancements in treating haematological, neurological, and metabolic disorders.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/cmc-vellore-hosts-11th-international-cell-and-gene-therapy-c.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Running through October 10, the conference features workshops covering disease modelling, organoids, and nucleic acid delivery. CGTCON 2026 aims to facilitate professional collaboration between clinicians, scientists, industry partners, and regulatory stakeholders to drive innovation in advanced therapeutics and manufacturing.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is well-structured and accurate, though it omits a few of the listed medical specialties (ocular, cardiovascular, dermatological) mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/cmc-to-organise-conference-on-gene-therapy-in-vellore/article71555717.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
