  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/world">world</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 3 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by BBC World, The Hindu World">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Cornell Students Voice Anger Over Alleged Gang Rape, Demand Accountability</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cornell University</span> <span>#Sexual Assault</span> <span>#Student Protest</span> <span>#Justice</span></div>
       <p>Cornell University students have expressed intense frustration at a public hearing regarding an alleged gang rape in 2024, with one student stating, “We’re absolutely ashamed of the events that happened on campus.” Students and faculty report that tension on campus has become palpable since the allegations resurfaced in recent weeks, as detailed by BBC World. The Ivy League school is currently trying to quell a &quot;firestorm&quot; on campus and beyond over its handling of the alleged incident, according to The Hindu World.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/cornell-students-voice-anger-over-alleged-gang-rape-demand-a.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The investigation into the incident has cast a “dark cloud” over the campus, stirring anger, concern over fraternity culture, and a significant backlash against the university’s handling of the situation. At Thursday’s student assembly, some labeled the perceived lack of justice a “disgrace,” criticizing the prestigious institution, which has defended its actions. Undergraduate Sophia Riley Sim told attendees, “We deserve to know that our institution values our safety more than its reputation,” adding that she had been too upset by the case to attend classes for the past week.</p><p>The accuser, identified anonymously as Jane Doe, filed a civil lawsuit against Cornell on September 16, alleging she was drugged and raped at a fraternity house during the incident two years prior. She claimed Cornell failed to protect her or adequately punish the men involved, who have been dubbed the “Cornell Seven.” Cornell has agreed to an independent investigation into the rape allegation and defended its previous handling, stating it conducted an “extensive investigation” that lasted several months and followed applicable federal civil rights law. The university noted that its hearing panel issued a “range of sanctions,” including expulsions and suspensions, but is legally prevented from publicly disclosing specific disciplinary outcomes.</p><p>In a significant development, New York Governor Kathy Hochul announced she had appointed state attorney general Letitia James as a special prosecutor in the case. Governor Hochul stated she had “lost faith” in Tompkins County District Attorney Matthew Van Houten, who was previously leading the investigation. Van Houten’s office initially concluded the evidence did not meet the legal threshold for charges but reopened a criminal investigation last week in light of the new civil complaint, a move Cornell supported.</p><p>An upcoming “Justice for Survivors” protest is planned at the university for October 5, advertised across campus, calling on Cornell to address alleged rape culture. Student organizers are demanding Cornell expel and revoke the degrees of the alleged perpetrators, rewrite policies around sexual assault punishments, initiate an external investigation of the university, and mandate prevention training for campus police.</p><p>Students and community members used Thursday’s assembly to vent their frustrations. A fourth-year student recalled the difficulty of living on campus in 2024 as rumors spread about Jane Doe, now feeling “overwhelmed” and “disappointed,” comparing the campus atmosphere to a “dark cloud.” Freshman Eliana Dolven-Miller expressed being “very disgusted to be here, to be paying this institution to be here.” Eeshaan Chaudhuri, the student assembly chair, affirmed the campus “stood with victims of sexual violence” and expressed shame over the events. The student group has also proposed a resolution calling on the university to release a written account of its handling of the alleged sexual assault, including evidence gathered and referrals to campus police. A faculty member described the campus mood as “dismal,” noting the challenges for staff not trained as therapists to navigate such discussions and recalling past issues with fraternity groups.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft synthesizes the provided information clearly, capturing the campus atmosphere and the specific demands of the student body accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm0e3ed1er1yo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC World</a></li><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/students-protest-cornells-response-to-gang-rape-complaint/article71549035.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
