     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>EPFO Issues Security Advisory Against Cyber Fraud</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Employees' Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) has issued a security advisory urging members to protect sensitive personal and financial data. The retirement fund body warned against sharing information like UAN, passwords, OTPs, Aadhaar, PAN, or bank details, emphasizing that it does not solicit such credentials via phone, email, or social media.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/epfo-issues-security-advisory-against-cyber-fraud.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Subscribers are advised to use only official portals and verify URLs to avoid phishing attempts. The EPFO stressed that users should refrain from clicking unverified links sent through SMS or email to maintain account security against emerging cybersecurity threats.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the security advisory and maintains a professional tone within the word limit.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/efpo-security-advisory-safeguard-your-account-personal-financial-info-cyber-fraud-dont-share-uan-pan-aadhaar-bank-detail-11791388079518.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
