     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Secures Asian Games Women's Hockey Gold, Ends 44-Year Wait and Qualifies for LA 2028 Olympics</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Women's Hockey</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#China</span></div>
       <p>India's women's hockey team claimed the gold medal at the Asian Games 2026 in Aichi-Nagoya, defeating World No. 4 China with a 1-0 victory in a hard-fought final. This monumental win marks India's 16th gold at the current Games and represents the nation's first women's hockey gold at the Asiad since 1982, concluding a 44-year wait. The triumph, spearheaded by the Salima Tete-led squad, also ensures direct qualification for the 2028 Olympics in Los Angeles.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/india-secures-asian-games-womens-hockey-gold-ends-44-year-wa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The decisive goal arrived early in the match, in the 10th minute of the first quarter, scored by Lalremsiami Hmarzote, who was notably playing her 200th game for India. The single goal proved sufficient, but not without significant challenges. A pivotal moment unfolded in the second quarter when China was awarded a penalty stroke. Indian veteran goalkeeper Savita Punia executed an &quot;incredible save,&quot; a moment characterized by NDTV Sports as the &quot;gold-defining moment,&quot; crucial for maintaining India's precarious lead. India held this crucial 1-0 lead at half-time, thanks to Lalremsiami's finish and Punia's save.</p><p>The second half continued with intense pressure. At the start of the third quarter, a penalty stroke initially awarded to China after the ball appeared to touch Navneet Kaur's foot was overturned upon referral, with China instead receiving a penalty corner. Captain Salima Tete made a &quot;brilliant block&quot; from this penalty corner, though she appeared to hurt her hand in the process. China continued to press, with a powerful low shot flashing across the goal and narrowly missing the target in the third quarter. India's defense held resolutely, preserving the one-goal advantage through the end of the third quarter.</p><p>In the final quarter, China intensified their attack, even substituting their goalkeeper for an outfielder in a bold move to create an all-out offensive with less than two minutes remaining. India had a rare counter-attack opportunity with no goalkeeper for China but could not convert. Despite China's efforts, including a shot that Savita Punia saved, India's defense remained impenetrable. The team, guided by coach Sjoerd Marijne, maintained their defensive resolve throughout the subsequent quarters, meticulously protecting their one-goal advantage against World No. 4 China, ultimately securing the victory.</p><p>This Asian Games gold medal culminates an extraordinary year for Indian women's hockey. Earlier this year, the team achieved its best-ever finish at a Women's Hockey World Cup, securing fifth place. Their dominant campaign at the Asian Games saw them win all seven matches, demonstrating formidable offensive power with 69 goals scored and exceptional defensive solidity by conceding only three goals throughout the tournament. The &quot;stunning achievement&quot; for Salima Tete, Sjoerd Marijne, and the team highlights a period of significant growth and success, setting a strong precedent for their upcoming Olympic challenge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is comprehensive and accurately incorporates all key details from the source, including specific match events and contextual statistics.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/hockey/india-vs-china-live-score-asian-games-2026-womens-hockey-final-ind-vs-chn-live-match-updates-aichi-nagoya-12129480#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
