     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ishaan S Sets World Record with Palk Strait Swim</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ishaan S</span> <span>#Palk Strait</span> <span>#World Record</span> <span>#Swimming</span></div>
       <p>Thirteen-year-old Ishaan S, who has autism and an intellectual disability, has achieved a world record by swimming 64-km across the Palk Strait. Ishaan, competing in the S14 category, completed the arduous journey from Dhanushkodi to Thalai Mannar in Sri Lanka and back, spending 18 hours and 50 minutes in the sea. He commenced his historic swim at 5 pm on September 29 from Dhanushkodi, reaching Thalai Mannar around 2 am on September 30. After a brief half-hour rest on a support boat, he began his return leg at 2:30 am, eventually arriving back at Dhanushkodi at 11:50 am.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/ishaan-s-sets-world-record-with-palk-strait-swim.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The World Book of World Records, London, has formally recognized Ishaan as the first and youngest special child globally in his category to accomplish this feat. The challenging attempt involved a comprehensive support team of 26 individuals, including swimmers, observers, lifeguards, and doctors, with two boats deployed to assist. Both Sri Lankan and Indian naval teams closely monitored the swimmers, and special permission was granted to cross the International Maritime Boundary Line specifically for this record attempt. For Ishaan's mother, A. Sharmila, a Chennai-based techie, this monumental swim transcends the mere achievement of a world record, representing a profound moment that counters the numerous rejections her autistic son faced in his early life.</p><p>Ishaan's path to the water began after exploring various activities like badminton, skating, yoga, and table tennis as a toddler, with swimming proving to enhance his focus significantly. Over the past two years, he underwent consistent training in Kovalam, building endurance through a 5-km Swimathon in Goa in 2025 and a 10-km swim in the Periyar River in Kochi. Prior to the Palk Strait endeavor, he dedicated five days to training at Dhanushkodi. His family's aspiration was not solely about winning but about demonstrating the immense possibilities when a child is given the right opportunity. Sharmila emphasized this, stating, &quot;We wanted to make him unique when everyone said it was not possible.&quot;</p><p>Beyond this world record, Ishaan already holds an impressive collection of eight gold and two silver medals from national and state-level competitions over the last two years. His mother recalls facing rejection from approximately 40 schools when trying to find an appropriate educational environment for him. However, Vel's Global School in Mogappair, where Ishaan now studies, has been a source of encouragement, even celebrating his record with a poster. Sharmila firmly believes, &quot;Given the opportunity, these children can really achieve.&quot; While Ishaan might not fully grasp the magnitude of his accomplishment, his mother notes, &quot;He just feels happy saying, 'I've done a world record.'&quot; He frequently asks her, &quot;Will friends come and clap for me? Will they accept me and take me in?&quot; Currently training at the SDAT Government Swimming Pool in Shenoy Nagar, Ishaan's next ambition is to compete internationally in the S14 category, a journey his mother is committed to supporting.</p><p>What to watch: Ishaan S aims to compete internationally in the S14 category.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a thorough and well-organized account of the swimmer's achievement, effectively incorporating the personal and technical details from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/swimming/from-rejection-to-world-record-ishaan-s-swims-across-the-palk-strait-12152976#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
