     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka Postal Circle to Sell 8,000 Philately Passports</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka Postal Circle will sell 8,000 philately passports on October 10 and 11 to mark National Postal Week. Passports cost ₹600 each and will be available at the Bengaluru GPO, Mangaluru, Mysuru, and Belagavi branches.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/karnataka-postal-circle-to-sell-8000-philately-passports.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sales are limited to a first-come, first-serve basis using physical tokens, with no online or advance bookings permitted. On October 10, 1,500 passports will be sold in Bengaluru and 500 each in the other three districts. On October 11, the allocation increases to 2,000 in Bengaluru and 1,000 per district elsewhere. Parking will be unavailable at the Bengaluru GPO during these dates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all key figures and dates provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/karnataka-postal-circle-to-sell-8000-philately-passports-on-october-10-and-11/article71556163.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
