     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kieron Pollard Joins Joburg Super Kings for R1.5 Million</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Joburg Super Kings signed West Indian all-rounder Kieron Pollard for his base price of R1.5 million at the SA20 2027 auction on October 7, 2026. The bid was unopposed, marking Pollard's transition from his former franchise, MI Cape Town.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/kieron-pollard-joins-joburg-super-kings-for-r15-million.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the same auction, the Super Kings also signed Zimbabwean bowler Blessing Muzarabani and Australian player Jason Rowles for R2.9 million. Held with a total team purse of R42 million, the auction saw active participation from four franchises. The Super Kings, coached by Albie Morkel, entered the event with six roster spots to fill and R20.6 million in remaining funds.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a dense and accurate summary of the auction results and franchise context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
