       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Meta Quest 3S Discounted to $297.49 During October Sales</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 128GB Meta Quest 3S is currently available for $297.49 at Amazon, Walmart, and Best Buy, marking a discount from its usual $349.99 price. This standalone VR headset utilizes the same chipset as the premium Quest 3 but maintains the lens and display specifications of the Quest 2.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/meta-quest-3s-discounted-to-29749-during-october-sales.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Purchases made through Amazon include three months of Horizon Plus, the &quot;Cardboard Monkenaut&quot; cosmetic set for Gorilla Tag, and 2,000 in-game &quot;Shiny Rocks.&quot; The device supports standalone functionality and PC-tethered gaming, offering a more accessible entry point for casual VR users compared to higher-end models.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the essential pricing, availability, and promotional details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/1006810/meta-quest-3s-prime-day-deal-sale" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
