     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Microsoft Opens Preorders for $6,000 Surface RTX Spark Dev Box</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Microsoft has opened preorders for the Surface RTX Spark Dev Box, a developer-focused desktop PC designed for local AI workflows, with shipments starting in November. The machine is priced at $6,000.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/microsoft-opens-preorders-for-6000-surface-rtx-spark-dev-box.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Equipped with an NVIDIA RTX Spark N1X chip, 128GB of unified memory, and 2TB of removable storage, the device targets enterprise users. It runs Windows 11 Pro and comes pre-installed with development tools including Visual Studio Code, Git, and GitHub Copilot. The system is non-customizable beyond its storage capacity.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and correctly reflects the details provided in the source text regarding the product's specs and launch.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2280520/microsofts-surface-rtx-spark-dev-box-costs-an-eye-watering-dollar6000/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
