      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/education">education</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NMC Mandates Licence to Practise Abroad for FMGE Eligibility</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Careers</span> <span>#NMC</span> <span>#FMGE</span></div>
       <p>The National Medical Commission (NMC) has recently tightened the eligibility criteria for the Foreign Medical Graduate Examination (FMGE), a development reported by India Today.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/nmc-mandates-licence-to-practise-abroad-for-fmge-eligibility.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Under the revised regulations, obtaining a licence to practice medicine abroad has been made mandatory for individuals seeking to appear for the FMGE. This new requirement impacts medical graduates who have completed their studies outside India and wish to practice in the country.</p><p>The move by the NMC aims to streamline the process and ensure that foreign medical graduates meet a specific standard of international practice before being considered eligible for the examination in India.</p><p>What to watch: How the new mandatory licence requirement impacts FMGE applicants.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core announcement regarding the NMC's new FMGE requirement using the provided source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
