       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Officials Seize One Tonne of PDS Rice in Arakkonam</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Civil Supplies officials and police seized one tonne of Public Distribution System (PDS) rice at a railway station in Arakkonam, Tamil Nadu, on Wednesday. The operation, directed by Collector N. Priya Ravichandran, resulted in the recovery of 22 bags of rice intended for public distribution. The shipment has been transferred to a Department of Civil Supplies godown in Ranipet.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/officials-seize-one-tonne-of-pds-rice-in-arakkonam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities initiated a probe after analyzing CCTV footage showing individuals loading the sacks onto a train. A case has been registered by Arakkonam police, and special teams have been formed to apprehend the suspects who escaped the scene.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is concise, accurate, and reflects all key details from the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/civil-supplies-officials-seizeone-tonne-of-pds-rice-in-ranipet/article71555700.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
