     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Online Harassment Targets Cornell Student and Misidentified Women</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Cornell University student who filed a lawsuit accusing seven fraternity members of gang rape is facing severe online harassment. Vigilantes attempting to identify the student have inadvertently targeted and harassed three other women who were falsely identified as the plaintiff.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/online-harassment-targets-cornell-student-and-misidentified-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Attorney Thomas Guiffra confirmed on Sunday that the actual Jane Doe is also under siege on social media, receiving numerous threats. The situation highlights the ongoing impact of targeted online vigilantism, as the plaintiff's legal team reports that their client is not doing well amidst the escalating digital abuse.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the central conflict and the attorney's statements accurately while remaining well within the length constraints.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/report/1006636/jane-doe-cornell-dox" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
