       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PM Modi marks 25 years in public office with nationwide BJP events</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi met veteran leader LK Advani on Wednesday to mark his 25-year milestone in public governance. Modi, who first became Gujarat Chief Minister on October 7, 2001, sought Advani's blessings while reflecting on his transition from state leadership to the Prime Minister's office.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/pm-modi-marks-25-years-in-public-office-with-nationwide-bjp-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To commemorate the anniversary, the BJP launched the 'Seva Sankalp Abhiyan' across India. Party workers held 'Viksit Bharat Sankalp Sabhas' and torch rallies to highlight the government's development agenda. Leaders including JP Nadda and Pushkar Singh Dhami participated in regional events, reinforcing the national goal of achieving a 'Viksit Bharat' by 2047.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Strong summary of the anniversary events and the timeline of the PM's public service.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
