     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>RBI Hikes Repo Rate by 25 BPS: Impact on Loans, Deposits, and Households</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#RBI</span> <span>#Repo Rate</span> <span>#Loans</span></div>
       <p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) announced a 25-basis-point increase in the repo rate on October 7, a move primarily aimed at curbing inflation. This adjustment directly impacts the interest rate at which the RBI lends short-term funds to banks. For ordinary savers and taxpayers, this typically translates to higher borrowing costs for various types of loans and potential adjustments to deposit rates, affecting household budgets and financial planning.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/rbi-hikes-repo-rate-by-25-bps-impact-on-loans-deposits-and-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A 25-basis-point hike means the repo rate has increased by 0.25 percentage points. This rise in borrowing costs for banks is often passed on to customers. Consequently, individuals with floating-rate loans, such as home, car, or personal loans linked to an external benchmark, may see their monthly instalments (EMIs) or overall repayment periods increase. However, the change in repayments is not necessarily immediate and depends on how individual lenders adjust their rates. It is crucial to understand that a 0.25 percentage point increase in the repo rate does not mean EMIs will rise by 25%.</p><p>Conversely, the repo rate hike can also influence savings and investment products. Banks may adjust their fixed deposit rates, potentially leading to higher returns for savers, though such increases are not guaranteed across all banks or products. Similarly, savings account interest rates might also see adjustments, reflecting changes in banks' funding costs. The RBI's decision balances the need to control rising prices with supporting economic growth, as costlier loans can also discourage business expansion. Following these announcements helps individuals anticipate financial changes and plan their household budgets more effectively.</p><p>What to watch: How individual banks adjust their lending and deposit rates in the coming weeks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the FAQ-style source text into a coherent, informative news piece that explains the impact of the rate hike clearly.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/rbi-hikes-repo-rate-by-25bps-what-it-means-and-how-it-impacts-you-all-faqs-answered-11791390783023.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
