     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-07 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shreyas Iyer hits maiden T20I century in India's victory over West Indies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India captain Shreyas Iyer scored an unbeaten 102 off 43 balls to lead his team to an 8-wicket victory against West Indies in Lucknow on October 6, 2026. Chasing a target of 172, India reached the total in 14.4 overs, fueled by Iyer's explosive innings of 10 fours and 6 sixes. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/shreyas-iyer-hits-maiden-t20i-century-in-indias-victory-over.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sunil Gavaskar praised the performance, noting that the century silenced recent criticism regarding Iyer's batting form. The captain shared an unbroken 137-run partnership with Ishan Kishan, who finished at 37 not out. Earlier, Indian bowlers Naman Dhir and Axar Patel restricted West Indies to 171 runs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief omits the source's explicit mention that this was Iyer's 11th T20I fifty, and it attributes a partnership total that is correct but misses the context of the bowlers' specific roles mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/strong-signal-shreyas-iyer-is-back-to-his-best-sunil-gavaskar-hails-india-skipper-after-maiden-t20i-ton-0951/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
