       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Supreme Court judge: Women's silence should not be price of family preservation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Supreme Court Justice Vikram Nath stated on Wednesday that women's silence regarding domestic violence must not be normalized or treated as a prerequisite for preserving family reputation. Speaking at a National Commission for Women conference, the judge emphasized that adjustment should not be expected when it involves enduring abuse. He noted that pressure to remain silent persists across all social and economic backgrounds, often stemming from the women's own families.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/supreme-court-judge-womens-silence-should-not-be-price-of-fa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Justice Nath asserted that women are equal citizens protected by the Constitution and entitled to live with dignity and security. He urged support systems to prioritize listening to victims rather than encouraging them to tolerate violence.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the essence of Justice Nath's speech and the context of the NCW conference accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/domestic-violence-justice-vikram-nath-says-women-must-be-heard-and-protected-ptag-3011891-2026-10-07?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
