     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tamil Nadu man claims ₹30-crore Thiruvonam Bumper lottery prize</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Tamil Nadu man named Sadiq has petitioned the Palakkad District Police Chief, claiming to be the winner of the Kerala government's ₹30-crore Thiruvonam Bumper lottery. Sadiq states he purchased the ticket at Palakkad Railway Junction but subsequently lost it in Sathyamangalam, Erode district.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/tamil-nadu-man-claims-30-crore-thiruvonam-bumper-lottery-pri.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To support his claim, Sadiq provided a photograph of the ticket stored on his mobile phone. Lottery officials and police are currently investigating the authenticity of the claim and determining if a digital image constitutes valid proof of ownership. The authorities have not yet confirmed the winner, noting that verification remains ongoing.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise summary of the reported lottery claim and current verification status.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/tamil-nadu-man-claims-30-crore-thiruvonam-bumper-lottery-prize/article71556319.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
