     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-07 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by News18 World, The Hindu World">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>UAE Labels Flydubai Cockpit Attack a 'Terrorist Act,' Praises Indian Pilot Smit Machchhar</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Flydubai</span> <span>#Cockpit Attack</span> <span>#Terrorism</span> <span>#Smit Machchhar</span></div>
       <p>The United Arab Emirates has officially characterized the recent attack aboard a Flydubai flight as a &quot;terrorist act,&quot; with UAE presidential adviser Anwar Gargash praising Indian Captain Smit Machchhar for his &quot;courage and responsibility&quot; during the incident. Gargash, in a post on X, stated that Machchhar &quot;deserves every appreciation&quot; for confronting what he termed a &quot;serious terrorist act and a potential disaster,&quot; describing him as a &quot;true hero&quot; for his professionalism under difficult circumstances. This marks the first public characterization of the event as a &quot;terrorist act&quot; by a senior UAE official, though a formal investigation into the motive is ongoing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-07/uae-labels-flydubai-cockpit-attack-a-terrorist-act-praises-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The incident occurred two days prior, when Flydubai flight FZ1073, en route from Dubai to Tel Aviv, was forced to divert to Saudi Arabia. According to Saudi authorities, the captain was attacked by his co-pilot in the cockpit, resulting in injuries to both pilots. The aircraft subsequently landed safely at Tabuk Airport. During the mid-air emergency, Captain Machchhar, despite his injuries, managed to open the cockpit door, enabling passengers and crew members to intervene and restrain the attacker. Other pilots on board then assisted in taking control of the aircraft. Machchhar was later transferred to the UAE for treatment and is currently recovering.</p><p>Beyond the UAE's official stance, international figures have also lauded Captain Machchhar. The Dubai Crown Prince praised the Indian pilot, stating, &quot;We are proud that he is part of our team… part of the story of our nation… and part of what the UAE stands for… a nation of compassion… a nation of peace… and a nation of life,&quot; as reported by The Hindu World. Furthermore, The Hindu World also noted that Netanyahu called Indian FlyDubai pilot Smit Machchhar &quot;hero of the entire world.&quot;</p><p>The UAE has initiated a formal investigation to examine the circumstances and motive behind the attack, including whether it was linked to &quot;any terrorist activity or purpose&quot; or involved &quot;prior planning or direction.&quot; The UAE has asserted its judicial authorities have jurisdiction over the case due to the aircraft's registration in the country. Gargash urged the public to avoid &quot;simplistic interpretations&quot; and &quot;conspiracy theories&quot; while stressing the importance of vigilance against extremism and terrorism.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent work; the article synthesizes the source material perfectly, maintaining accuracy while including the additional context from cited outlets.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/uae-calls-flydubai-incident-terrorist-act-praises-indian-pilot-smit-machchhar-10364751.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/flydubai-attack-dubai-crown-prince-praises-indian-pilot-machchhar/article71540812.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
